### Purpose

A launcher for pre-made Claude Code agents in isolated Docker containers — each persona has its own model, parameters, and instructions, but shares OAuth credentials, workspace, slash commands, status line, and toolchain caches. Supports multiple persistent sessions per agent and resumes prior conversations automatically.

### Tech Stack

- Python 3.10+ on host: `run.py` (entry point) + `launch/` package (`agents_lib`, `menu_picker`, `audit`).
- Host Python deps: `prompt_toolkit` (full-screen picker UI), `python-dotenv` (`.conf` parsing).
- Docker + Docker Compose v2; one container per launched instance.
- Debian Bookworm slim base; container installs Claude Code (`claude.ai/install.sh`), Rust (`rustup`), `uv`, plus `ripgrep`, `git`, `curl`, `build-essential`, `pkg-config`, `libssl-dev`.
- No tests, no CI, no lockfile.

